{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And see and make.</b> See here on the mountain the pattern that I show you — this tells that Moses found the making of the menorah difficult until the Holy One, blessed be He, showed him a menorah of fire (ibid. 29)." "<b>That you are shown.</b> As the Targum renders: דְּאַתְּ מִתְחֲזֵי בְּטוּרָא. If it were pointed מַרְאֶה, with a patach, its meaning would be 'you show to others.' Now that it is pointed with a chasef-kamatz, its meaning is דְּאַתְּ מִתְחֲזֵי — that others show to you (for the pointing distinguishes between the one who makes and the one who is made)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:37.060169330Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}